'' RUN: STRING -> WSTRING decodes valid UTF-8 as UTF-8 on Windows (then the ANSI code page),
'' so std/chrono's UTF-8 locale names reach a `const wstring ptr` (sys/win Msg) intact --
'' 'miércoles', not 'miÃ©rcoles'. Asserts UTF-16 code units; locale-independent. Needs the
'' runtime of this commit, so it passes only once the toolchain is repackaged (it links the
'' packaged libfb.a).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/utf8-to-wstring.tiko -o tests/codegen/utf8towstring.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/utf8towstring.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/utf8towstring.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ok
